# function: parse_project_slug

The inverse of `project_slug`: given a slug such as `"gh/my-org/my-repo"` or `"circleci/<orgUUID>/<projectUUID>"`, returns an object with `vcs_type`, `org` and `project` attributes. Errors if the slug does not have exactly three non-empty, `/`-separated segments — a shape mismatch that would otherwise reach the API as a confusing 404.

Useful for pulling a slug apart that arrived as a single string (for example from an existing resource's `project_slug` attribute, or a data source list keyed by slug) when only one segment — usually `org` — is actually needed.

